<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
  body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; }
  h1 { color: #1A365D; font-size: 24px; border-bottom: 2px solid #ED8936; padding-bottom: 5px; }
  h2 { color: #2C4A7C; font-size: 18px; margin-top: 20px; }
  .callout { background-color: #FEF3C7; border-left: 4px solid #ED8936; padding: 10px; margin: 15px 0; }
  .quiz { background-color: #F8FAFC; padding: 15px; border: 1px solid #E2E8F0; border-radius: 8px; margin: 15px 0; }
  .meta { background-color: #E0F2FE; padding: 10px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 12px; color: #0369A1; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 15px 0; }
  th { background-color: #1A365D; color: white; padding: 10px; text-align: left; }
  td { border: 1px solid #CBD5E1; padding: 10px; }
  .instruction { color: #64748B; font-size: 12px; font-style: italic; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="meta">
  <strong>TEACHER INSTRUCTIONS:</strong> Follow the structure below. The parser uses these exact tags to build your interactive lesson.
</div>

<h1>Lesson Title Here (e.g., Introduction to Chemistry)</h1>

<p><strong>COVER IMAGE:</strong> https://example.com/your-cover-image.jpg</p>
<p><strong>VIDEO URL:</strong> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ</p>

<h2>1. Section Heading</h2>
<p>This is a normal paragraph. Write your lesson content here. Keep it clear and easy to read for students.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Key Takeaway</strong><br>
  > Start your sentence with a greater-than symbol to make a highlighted callout box like this. Use this for important notes.
</div>

<h2>2. Formulas</h2>
<p>Use the [FORMULA] tag to insert math or chemistry formulas.</p>
<p>[FORMULA] 2n^2 [/FORMULA]</p>

<h2>3. Data Tables</h2>
<p>Just use Word's standard Insert > Table feature. The parser will turn your table into a formatted data block.</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Shell</th><th>Max Electrons</th><th>Formula</th></tr>
  <tr><td>K</td><td>2</td><td>2(1)²</td></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>8</td><td>2(2)²</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>4. Quizzes</h2>
<p class="instruction">Use the exact format below for quizzes. Include the question, choices, the correct answer number, and an explanation.</p>

<div class="quiz">
  <strong>Q.1: What is the charge of a neutron?</strong><br>
  A) +1<br>
  B) -1<br>
  C) 0<br>
  <strong>Answer: C</strong><br>
  <em>Description: Neutrons have no charge. They are neutral particles found in the nucleus.</em>
</div>

<div class="quiz">
  <strong>Q.2: Which particle determines the atomic number?</strong><br>
  A) Neutron<br>
  B) Proton<br>
  C) Electron<br>
  <strong>Answer: B</strong><br>
  <em>Description: The number of protons defines the element and its atomic number.</em>
</div>

</body>
</html>
